

Cart requirement:

1. User can add maximum 10 items in the cart

2. If cart is empty "Checkout" button should be disabled

3. if cart reaches 10 items user gets popup message like "Cart is full"

4. if cart is empty the page should display "Your cart is empty, add items

   to checkout"

5. Product can be added to cart with or without login

6. At the time of checkout cart will ask for user to login if not logged in



Flow:

Home -> search -> product -> add to cart -> checkout -> Login ->payment

Login -> search -> product ->add to cart -> checkout -> payment





Test Case 1

Test Case ID: TC001

Test Scenario: Verify that user can add a product to cart without login.

Precondition: User is on the Home page and not logged in.

Test Steps:

Search for a product.
Select the product.
Click Add to Cart.
Open the Cart.

Expected Result:
Product should be added successfully to the cart.

Test Case 2

Test Case ID: TC002

Test Scenario: Verify that user can add a product to cart after login.

Precondition: User is logged in and is on the Home page.

Test Steps:

Search for a product.
Select the product.
Click Add to Cart.
Open the Cart.

Expected Result:
Product should be added successfully to the cart.

Test Case 3

Test Case ID: TC003

Test Scenario: Verify that maximum 10 items can be added to the cart.

Precondition: User is on the Home page.

Test Steps:

Search for a product.
Select the product.
Click Add to Cart.
Repeat the process until 10 items are added.

Expected Result:
User should be able to add maximum 10 items to the cart.

Test Case 4

Test Case ID: TC004

Test Scenario: Verify that user cannot add more than 10 items.

Precondition: Cart already contains 10 items.

Test Steps:

Search for another product.
Select the product.
Click Add to Cart.

Expected Result:
Product should not be added and "Cart is full" popup message should be displayed.

Test Case 5

Test Case ID: TC005

Test Scenario: Verify Checkout button when cart is empty.

Precondition: Cart is empty.

Test Steps:

Open the Cart page.
Check the Checkout button.

Expected Result:
Checkout button should be disabled.

Test Case 6

Test Case ID: TC006

Test Scenario: Verify empty cart message.

Precondition: Cart is empty.

Test Steps:

Open the Cart page.

Expected Result:
Message "Your cart is empty, add items to checkout" should be displayed.

Test Case 7

Test Case ID: TC007

Test Scenario: Verify checkout asks for login when user is not logged in.

Precondition: Product is added to cart and user is not logged in.

Test Steps:

Open the Cart.
Click Checkout.

Expected Result:
User should be redirected to the Login page.

Test Case 8

Test Case ID: TC008

Test Scenario: Verify user can proceed to payment after login.

Precondition: Product is added to cart and user is on the Login page.

Test Steps:

Enter valid username.
Enter valid password.
Click Login.
Continue checkout.

Expected Result:
User should be redirected to the Payment page.
